{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787023068203664002,"compiled_state":{"alias":"diamond-flavoured-esok","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":5,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"330cd659f57231cd36e495218e215f63c7ef69722edc8f3e780bf8d2b177d49c","event_uuid":"bcce2072-1dfe-4559-8ee3-04a03c3aa2f8","position":{"commit_sha":"bc18eb44c850110d2e492a8d5535326532c14a1b","position":"1787022636066935001-bcce2072-1dfe-4559-8ee3-04a03c3aa2f8"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"87c57e1d5e5e2fc6266752e46022e7264b65cb6f15d48855e708138e6a56edb4","event_uuid":"992726ed-8aa3-4f37-9ee8-3eda1e5e1054","position":{"commit_sha":"f447eb957a742f002c542080eff7d096f7bcdcf0","position":"1787022688641145001-992726ed-8aa3-4f37-9ee8-3eda1e5e1054"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"e4c8bc1423b1cb86cf1cfb1f3bfa2c52c4ef96a4031be4f950dc8773ac9d409d","event_uuid":"07831f33-df5c-431e-a1c4-8b751cf7fde8","position":{"commit_sha":"c8b449110fc20c6c5516d79e3170d78d9dec15b3","position":"1787022928399306001-07831f33-df5c-431e-a1c4-8b751cf7fde8"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"a9b48cf7330c78b3548f5362c5ebe945f30a905e632e9bcb4164482bb5dc7395","event_uuid":"86082e55-43eb-41c7-afd3-77fede36c50f","position":{"commit_sha":"e38e80d9ec8cb9126cb867d897c178f7ecf96665","position":"1787023026012170001-86082e55-43eb-41c7-afd3-77fede36c50f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"191e72c1ebe38152de7eb194aa09d3844a4ce56b026cb1626a08f798e2ac2f14","event_uuid":"c9ab69e0-8d62-403d-8d0f-7316454ee095","position":{"commit_sha":"e22abcef582009076de4f4d448a99e7c39f9ae93","position":"1787023068203664001-c9ab69e0-8d62-403d-8d0f-7316454ee095"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787022636066935001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"992726ed-8aa3-4f37-9ee8-3eda1e5e1054","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"59b0-d1b9-ad94-4339"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nAfter operation-family cutovers, leaving generic `_call_with_retry`, `_best_effort`, duck-typed production dispatch, or legacy write routes active would preserve retry multiplication and allow future code to bypass the coordinator. Preview/log consumers also need a stable versioned contract for lifecycle and deferred outcomes before expand can contract.\n\n## Outcome\nFinish the expand/contract migration: route every supported live mutation through typed plans/coordinator/adapters, remove obsolete physical-retry and write fallbacks, fail loudly for unsupported production paths, and seal manifests, logs, pass cursor/tallies, documentation, and local verified-fake validation. Preserve existing mutation shape while making lifecycle/retry/fuse outcomes explicit and observable.\n\n## Plan\n1. Inventory every Cloud/DC mutation leaf and prove it reaches the typed coordinator. Remove generic whole-operation retry, `_best_effort` write swallowing, production class-name/duck fallbacks, and duplicate SDK/adapter retry owners.\n2. Keep compatibility only at serialized/public read boundaries. An unsupported live action raises a typed pre-effect error; tests may use explicit fakes implementing the declared protocol.\n3. Finalize versioned preview/manifest sections for lifecycle intents, logical/physical attempts, delay source/value, budgets, scope, disposition, `retry_not_before`, fuse state, and exact per-ticket/pass outcomes. Redact secrets and bound diagnostic size.\n4. Advance cursor/baseline/binding state only for proven postconditions. Deferred, failed, skipped, and commit-unknown work remains eligible for later re-observation and is never reported as applied.\n5. Add ADR/docs for retry ownership, failure taxonomy, scoped fuse, label-first create containment, explicit behavior deltas, expand/contract rollback, and future adapter obligations. Run portable verified-fake Cloud/DC end-to-end tests; retain bounded live probes as optional operator evidence.\n\n## Testing (RED → GREEN)\n- A dispatch census test enumerates every `MutationDirection`/`MutationAction` and provider route, asserting one typed owner or an intentional pre-effect unsupported error.\n- End-to-end fake Cloud/DC passes cover mixed success, transient recovery, long-delay deferral, permanent ticket failure, auth/provider stop, fuse open/reset, create containment, restart, and delivery failure.\n- Golden preview/log/manifest tests pin existing mutation fields plus additive versioned sections, redaction, bounded diagnostics, and exact tally/exit semantics.\n- Static/string and runtime poison tests fail if removed legacy helpers or hidden retries are reachable from production.\n\n## Compatibility / rollback\nContract only after shadow parity and each family cutover test passes. A pre-contract release can revert per-family routing; after removal, rollback is a code revert that re-observes remote state and never compensates by deleting successful Jira work. Stored ticket/binding/event formats are unchanged; additive manifest fields are versioned and ignorable.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A route census proves every supported Cloud/DC mutation uses exactly one typed coordinator/adapter path and no hidden SDK, generic wrapper, `_best_effort`, or duck-typed production fallback remains reachable.\n- [ ] Unsupported production actions fail before local/remote effects with a typed provider-neutral error.\n- [ ] Preview, manifest, and logs preserve existing mutation fields and add versioned redacted logical-attempt, lifecycle, delay/budget, disposition, fuse, and `retry_not_before` data.\n- [ ] Cursor, baseline, and binding state advance only for proven postconditions; deferred/failed/skipped/commit-unknown work is never counted as applied and remains recoverable next pass.\n- [ ] Portable verified-fake Cloud/DC end-to-end suites cover the approved taxonomy, retry envelope, fuse, create containment, restart, and partial-outcome behavior without external credentials.\n- [ ] ADR and operator docs record ownership, intentional behavior changes, future adapter contract, no-dual-write cutover, and rollback that never deletes successful Jira work.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/applier.py","reason":"Remove legacy generic retry and write dispatch fallbacks."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/batch_dispatch.py","reason":"Remove obsolete whole-operation retry routes."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/manifest_renderer.py","reason":"Seal versioned lifecycle, retry, fuse, and outcome output."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/reconcile.py","reason":"Make coordinator results authoritative for state advancement and exit status."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/last_pass.py","reason":"Persist exact deferred/failed/recovered pass outcome semantics."},{"path":"docs/adr/0100-reconciler-operation-coordination.md","reason":"Record retry ownership, taxonomy, fuse, containment, and cutover decisions."},{"path":"docs/adr/README.md","reason":"Index the operation-coordination ADR."},{"path":"docs/architecture.md","reason":"Document the planner/coordinator/adapter dependency direction."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_coordinator_route_census.py","reason":"Prove one typed owner or fail-loud unsupported behavior for every route."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_reconciler_coordinator.py","reason":"Portable verified-fake Cloud/DC end-to-end validation."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","59b0-d1b9-ad94-4339"],["parent","4217-d1d6-370b-4e98"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"4217-d1d6-370b-4e98","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["rp03","reconciler","cutover","observability","tdd"],"ticket_id":"3350-90b1-2651-4c50","ticket_type":"story","title":"RP-03 S5 — Complete coordinator cutover and remove legacy write fallbacks","verify_commands":[{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_coordinator_route_census.py","dd_id":"AC1-AC2","dd_text":"Complete typed route census and fail-loud unsupported paths"},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_preview_lifecycle_intents.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_live_mode_failure_tally.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_bridge_canonical_manifest.py","dd_id":"AC3-AC4","dd_text":"Versioned output, exact state advancement, and pass outcome semantics"},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/interfaces/store/test_reconciler_coordinator.py","dd_id":"AC5","dd_text":"Portable verified-fake Cloud/DC end-to-end coordinator behavior"},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/test_check_docs_index.py tests/scripts/test_check_adr_numbers.py","dd_id":"AC6","dd_text":"ADR numbering and documentation index integrity"}]},"source_event_uuids":["bcce2072-1dfe-4559-8ee3-04a03c3aa2f8","992726ed-8aa3-4f37-9ee8-3eda1e5e1054","07831f33-df5c-431e-a1c4-8b751cf7fde8","86082e55-43eb-41c7-afd3-77fede36c50f","c9ab69e0-8d62-403d-8d0f-7316454ee095"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787023068203664002,"uuid":"02fc9070-0824-4683-965d-865048eea273"}